 <p class="note">Applicability: written for fixed- and rotary-wing pilots of every service. Everything outside the sim panel is from the Air Force manual, the FAA's manual, or the Navy's instrument training instructions, with type-specific numbers left out: procedures are given in generic form, and your aircraft's numbers come from its flight manual. The Navy's NATOPS instrument flight manual and the Army's instrument publications could not be read for this revision, so no Army rules are included, and Navy rules beyond the training instructions and the Air Force manual's Navy airfield holding speed are not covered. Your service's rules, the aircraft's flight manual and current FLIP govern.</p>

